ion","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:ea4acbbd449c62f4556f49de313d5165013b1b8a978b1344e2711a34d057ad08","file":"preprints/Entropy-and-Face-Dimension-of-the-Perfect-Matching-Polytope-September-23-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":201,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"59c34ad8be5335b8ec761ed21ddb30ed620c8433e8359268c1adcb1502de2c37","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Entropy-and-Face-Dimension-of-the-Perfect-Matching-Polytope-September-23-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:ea4acbbd449c62f4556f49de313d5165013b1b8a978b1344e2711a34d057ad08","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Entropy-and-Face-Dimension-of-the-Perfect-Matching-Polytope-September-23-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L201"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\\label{thm:algorithm-guarantee}\nThere is one uniform deterministic algorithm which, on a graph on $n$\nvertices with nonnegative binary integer pair multiplicities, returns an\ninteger $A\\ge0$ satisfying\n\\[\n                         N(G)/512^n\\le A\\le N(G).\n\\]\nIts running time and output length are polynomial in the input bit length.\nIn particular, $A=0$ exactly when $N(G)=0$. The guarantee includes a compact\ninput consisting of binary $n$ and a list of positive pair records."}
